{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1174380-bloodline-praenuntiator","id":1174380,"title":"Bloodline - Praenuntiator","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-08T16:09:24-08:00","id":1174380,"title":"Bloodline - Praenuntiator","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Praenuntiator</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>You think you're smart, don't you? You think you know what's going to happen? Well you don't. I've seen what's coming this way, and it'll tear you down. Your connections, your ghouls, your childe, nothing will save you. But, for a price, I'll tell you what's coming.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Praenuntiators are a bloodline founded at the height of the Roman Empire. Hailing from an ancient Julii's advisory, they offered advice to many Princes in the Camarilla, telling the future in exchange for a safe haven. However, it is not uncommon for a Praenuntiator to be cast out if they bring bad news.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mind of an Auger receives pictures of things that are yet to come, oftentimes, this is overlooked or forgotten. They gift, or curse as some would say, comes naturally to them, even if they possess no Auspex. The visions serve as leverage oftentimes, and, if pleasing, are sold in exchange for favors.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Background:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Praenuntiators origins are shrouded in mystery. Around 200 B.C., an unknown Daeva drank a mortal dry. If it was to escape the clan's curse or not is unknown, but what is known is that the mortal became a Revenant. The Revenant, who's true name is lost to time, was uplifted by a Mekhet. The Mekhet is known to have disappeared, and was presumably diablerised by his new chide.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Many years later, the first Praenuntiator was known to have fled into a woods, and return with memories not constrained to time. Some Kindred scholars presume that a Fae or Demon gave him the ability, but the majority of the bloodline rejects this. Most claim it is their strength of will that gifts them with the visions, not an external force. Several eccentric scholars claim they are tapping into the memories of everything through a mixture of Majesty and Auspex.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They stayed in Rome until the fall of the Camarilla, and afterwards they scattered throughout Europe, serving as occultist and prophets. Their numbers remained small, due to the recklessness brought by the Embrace. They served in an advisory role wherever profit could be made, staying long enough to take the profit and leave. This caused many to move to the Americas</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Becoming:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Praenuntiators are embraced for their wits and knowledge. Who better to know the future than one who can interpret it and utilize it. They do not take the Embrace lightly, for most die from the fearlessness of knowing everything.They keep the new childe close, hoping that they will be worth the investment. Oftentimes they only Embrace after heavily reading the future, studying if their future childe would die, only for their actions to change the childes fate.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In the Danse Macabre:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Praenuntiator act as advisors, aiding rulers who are likely already on the right track or will be. They are drawn to success like a moth to the flames. This makes them seem more reliable, giving them lofty positions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Individually, many Praenuntiator use their talents to become successful in their chosen field. They usually soar in whatever they do, but like Icarus they are doomed to fall. Their sense of power sends them to an early grave, as many develop false sense of invincibility.When Praenuntiator join a covenant, it is usually one they see themselves most successful in. This makes them equally spread between all the covenants.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Nickname:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Augurs</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Clan:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Mekhet</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Bane:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Augurs' visions tend to lead into recklessness. In addition to the Mekhet clan weakness, a Praenuntiator's Defense is capped by her Humanity</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Gift:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Once per scene, a Praenuntiator may spend a Willpower to know the future. They roll Wits + Occult. Success means you ask the GM a number of yes or no question equal to success. The GM must answer truthfully. Dramatic failure means you get a falsely answered question.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Bloodline Disciplines:</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, Majesty</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23575-mrmonsterguy18","name":"MrMonsterGuy18","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T00:32:39-08:00","id":1174490,"title":"","content":"Nice take on the seer concept. Something which I think could be expanded on is the concept of their foresight hindering them as in lowering their Defense and essentially sending them to their deaths, as I understood it, somewhat early.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T04:40:22-08:00","id":1174521,"title":"","content":"I'd give them a real weakness. Something along the lines that their questions must center on or prominently feature themselves or they are emphatically blind to the future when it comes to making predictions directly about themselves. (Ties into feeding the narcissism of Majesty use.)<br /> Either scenario would encourage their marks to want to keep them close and involve them in their schemes only to discard the fortune teller when he acquires too many enemies.<br /> It is also an effective limitation that prevents them from shitting all over every scene by knowing absolutely everything that will happen before it happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}